# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write, upload, and run your first managed workflow, then get its results."
msgstr "Isulat, i-upload, at patakbuhin ang una mong managed workflow, pagkatapos ay kunin ang mga resulta nito."

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deploy your first managed workflow"
msgstr "I-deploy ang una mong managed workflow"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"guides/deploy-first-managed-workflow.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore writefile */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/*\n"
"  DO NOT EDIT THIS CELL!!!\n"
"  This cell's content is generated automatically by a script. Anything you add\n"
"  here will be removed next time the notebook is run. To add new content, create\n"
"  a new cell before or after this one.\n"
"*/}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Package versions\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mga bersyon ng package\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code on this page was developed using the following requirements.\n"
"We recommend using these versions or newer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang code sa pahinang ito ay binuo gamit ang mga sumusunod na requirement.\n"
"Inirerekomenda naming gamitin ang mga bersyong ito o mas bago.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Use this page to upload a workflow, run it, and get its result. The example workflow optimizes and simulates a Qiskit circuit. It simulates the circuit on classical hardware, so it does not use QPU time.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Gamitin ang pahinang ito para mag-upload ng workflow, patakbuhin ito, at kunin ang resulta nito. Ino-optimize at sinisimulate ng halimbawang workflow ang isang Qiskit circuit. Sinisimulate nito ang circuit sa classical hardware, kaya hindi ito gumagamit ng QPU time.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you begin, [install the client package and authenticate](/guides/install-managed-workflows).\n"
msgstr "Bago ka magsimula, [i-install ang client package at mag-authenticate](/guides/install-managed-workflows).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Use AI skills (optional)\">\n"
"To deploy your own code with help from an AI assistant, use the AI skills in the [Qiskit Function templates repository](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-function-templates).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Gumamit ng AI skills (opsyonal)\">\n"
"Para i-deploy ang sarili mong code na may tulong ng AI assistant, gamitin ang mga AI skill sa [Qiskit Function templates repository](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-function-templates).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write a workflow {#write-a-workflow}"
msgstr "Sumulat ng workflow {#write-a-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the folder structure {#create-the-folder-structure}"
msgstr "Gawin ang folder structure {#create-the-folder-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow is a folder of Python files with one entrypoint file. A managed workflow uploads everything in the folder, up to 50 MB, and runs the entrypoint as a script. Because a workflow uploads the whole folder, keep your local files, such as `deploy.ipynb`, outside the folder. Create the following layout:\n"
msgstr "Ang managed workflow ay isang folder ng mga Python file na may isang entrypoint file. Ina-upload ng managed workflow ang lahat ng nasa folder, hanggang 50 MB, at pinapatakbo ang entrypoint bilang script. Dahil ina-upload ng workflow ang buong folder, panatilihin ang iyong mga local file, tulad ng `deploy.ipynb`, sa labas ng folder. Gawin ang sumusunod na layout:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write the hello world entrypoint {#write-the-hello-world-entrypoint}"
msgstr "Isulat ang hello world entrypoint {#write-the-hello-world-entrypoint}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entrypoint reads a circuit, optimizes and simulates it, and saves the counts and two-qubit depth. Save the following code as `source_files/hello_world.py`:\n"
msgstr "Binabasa ng entrypoint ang isang circuit, ino-optimize at sinisimulate ito, at sine-save ang mga count at ang two-qubit depth. I-save ang sumusunod na code bilang `source_files/hello_world.py`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"If you read this page as a notebook, the code cell for `hello_world.py` starts with the `%%writefile` [magic command](https://ipython.readthedocs.io/en/stable/interactive/magics.html#cellmagic-writefile). When you run this cell, it saves the code to the file instead of running the code.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Kung binabasa mo ang pahinang ito bilang notebook, nagsisimula ang code cell para sa `hello_world.py` sa `%%writefile` [magic command](https://ipython.readthedocs.io/en/stable/interactive/magics.html#cellmagic-writefile). Kapag pinatakbo mo ang cell na ito, sine-save nito ang code sa file sa halip na patakbuhin ang code.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entrypoint uses three functions from `qiskit_serverless`:\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang entrypoint ng tatlong function mula sa `qiskit_serverless`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`get_arguments()` returns the keyword arguments that you pass to `run()`, as a dictionary. Each value must be JSON-serializable, or an object that the client can encode, such as a `QuantumCircuit`. Encoded objects arrive as the same objects that you passed.\n"
msgstr "Ibinabalik ng `get_arguments()` ang mga keyword argument na ipinapasa mo sa `run()`, bilang dictionary. Dapat JSON-serializable ang bawat value, o isang object na kayang i-encode ng client, tulad ng `QuantumCircuit`. Dumarating ang mga na-encode na object bilang parehong mga object na ipinasa mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` sets the detailed status `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE`, which you can see while the job runs. See [Report progress with update_status()](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status).\n"
msgstr "Itinatakda ng `update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` ang detalyadong status na `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE`, na makikita mo habang tumatakbo ang job. Tingnan ang [Report progress with update_status()](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`save_result()` stores a JSON-serializable value that you read later with `job.result()`. The workflow returns the counts as a dictionary and the two-qubit depth of the optimized circuit as an integer.\n"
msgstr "Iniimbak ng `save_result()` ang isang JSON-serializable na value na babasahin mo mamaya gamit ang `job.result()`. Ibinabalik ng workflow ang mga count bilang dictionary at ang two-qubit depth ng na-optimize na circuit bilang integer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output, such as the two-qubit depth, goes to the job's logs. To add timestamps and log levels, use the `logging` module. See [Write logs and handle errors](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors).\n"
msgstr "Anumang isinusulat ng workflow sa standard output, tulad ng two-qubit depth, ay napupunta sa mga log ng job. Para magdagdag ng mga timestamp at log level, gamitin ang `logging` module. Tingnan ang [Write logs and handle errors](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the workflow {#upload-the-workflow}"
msgstr "I-upload ang workflow {#upload-the-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In your local notebook, run the following code from the `hello_world_project` folder. The code connects with your saved account, defines the workflow, and uploads it. `entrypoint` is the file that the workflow runs, and `working_dir` is the folder that you upload:\n"
msgstr "Sa iyong local notebook, patakbuhin ang sumusunod na code mula sa folder na `hello_world_project`. Kumokonekta ang code gamit ang iyong naka-save na account, dine-define ang workflow, at ina-upload ito. Ang `entrypoint` ay ang file na pinapatakbo ng workflow, at ang `working_dir` ay ang folder na ina-upload mo:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the workflow with inputs {#run-the-workflow-with-inputs}"
msgstr "Patakbuhin ang workflow gamit ang mga input {#run-the-workflow-with-inputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Construct a three-qubit GHZ circuit to pass to `hello_world` as an input:\n"
msgstr "Gumawa ng three-qubit GHZ circuit na ipapasa sa `hello_world` bilang input:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run `hello_world` with the circuit and the number of shots as keyword arguments. The argument names match the keys that the entrypoint reads with `get_arguments()`:\n"
msgstr "Patakbuhin ang `hello_world` gamit ang circuit at ang bilang ng mga shot bilang mga keyword argument. Tumutugma ang mga pangalan ng argument sa mga key na binabasa ng entrypoint gamit ang `get_arguments()`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`run()` returns a `Job` after the workflow queues the job. It does not wait for the job to run. The job continues in the cloud after you close your Python session. To find it again later, list your recent jobs with `client.jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "Nagbabalik ang `run()` ng `Job` pagkatapos i-queue ng workflow ang job. Hindi ito naghihintay na tumakbo ang job. Magpapatuloy ang job sa cloud pagkatapos mong isara ang iyong Python session. Para hanapin ito ulit mamaya, ilista ang iyong mga kamakailang job gamit ang `client.jobs()`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: add the web UI for job history when it is available. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the status, result, and logs {#get-the-status-result-and-logs}"
msgstr "Kunin ang status, result, at mga log {#get-the-status-result-and-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Immediately after you call `run()`, the status is usually `QUEUED`:\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos mismo ng pagtawag mo sa `run()`, karaniwang `QUEUED` ang status:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The status changes from `QUEUED` to `INITIALIZING`, `RUNNING`, and then `DONE`.\n"
msgstr "Nagbabago ang status mula `QUEUED` patungong `INITIALIZING`, `RUNNING`, at pagkatapos ay `DONE`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.result()` waits until the job ends, then returns the value that the workflow passed to `save_result()`:\n"
msgstr "Naghihintay ang `job.result()` hanggang matapos ang job, pagkatapos ay ibinabalik ang value na ipinasa ng workflow sa `save_result()`:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/managed-workflows/deploy-first-managed-workflow/extracted-outputs/b4e7a2fe-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/managed-workflows/deploy-first-managed-workflow/extracted-outputs/b4e7a2fe-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can read the logs while the job runs. The workflow uploads new lines about every 15 seconds. The logs include the line that the workflow printed:\n"
msgstr "Puwede mong basahin ang mga log habang tumatakbo ang job. Nag-a-upload ang workflow ng mga bagong linya tuwing mga 15 segundo. Kasama sa mga log ang linyang pinrint ng workflow:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update the workflow {#update-the-workflow}"
msgstr "I-update ang workflow {#update-the-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To change a workflow, edit its files and call `upload()` again with the same `title`. The new upload replaces the earlier one, and jobs that already started are not affected.\n"
msgstr "Para baguhin ang isang workflow, i-edit ang mga file nito at tawagin muli ang `upload()` gamit ang parehong `title`. Pinapalitan ng bagong upload ang nauna, at hindi naaapektuhan ang mga job na nagsimula na.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fields such as `arguments_schema` and `sizes_map` keep their stored values when you omit them from the new upload.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga field tulad ng `arguments_schema` at `sizes_map` ay nananatili ang kanilang mga naka-store na value kapag inalis mo ang mga ito sa bagong upload.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Define inputs and outputs](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs) to learn which argument and result types a workflow supports.\n"
"- [Declare dependencies](/guides/managed-workflow-dependencies) to use more Python packages in your workflow.\n"
"- [Run quantum jobs from a workflow](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows) to run your circuits on a QPU, report each stage, and track the QPU jobs.\n"
"- [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) to learn all job statuses, debug a failed job, and find a job later.\n"
"- To start from working code, deploy one of the [Qiskit Function templates](/guides/qiskit-function-templates), or adapt a template for your own workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Mga Rekomendasyon\">\n"
"- [Define inputs and outputs](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs) para malaman kung anong mga uri ng argument at result ang sinusuportahan ng workflow.\n"
"- [Declare dependencies](/guides/managed-workflow-dependencies) para gumamit ng mas maraming Python package sa iyong workflow.\n"
"- [Run quantum jobs from a workflow](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows) para patakbuhin ang iyong mga circuit sa isang QPU, i-report ang bawat stage, at subaybayan ang mga QPU job.\n"
"- [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) para malaman ang lahat ng job status, i-debug ang bigong job, at hanapin ang isang job mamaya.\n"
"- Para magsimula sa gumaganang code, i-deploy ang isa sa mga [Qiskit Function templates](/guides/qiskit-function-templates), o i-adapt ang isang template para sa sarili mong workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
